don't raise money until you have a real  business and you have some momentum  behind you otherwise you're going to get  killed on your valuation and it's going  to chew up all of your time not giving  you anything that to work with the build  your business hi I'm Evan Carmichael I  believe that hungry entrepreneurs  deserve help and today maintain a  question from one of my newsletter  readers Norman who wrote in the say good  afternoon mr. Carmichael my name is  Norman I'm a novice entrepreneur I've  been trying to get into entrepreneurship  for a little over three years now i  graduated college you want to start my  business I need five thousand dollars  for capital for software and coaching I  know it doesn't seem a lot but I can't  come across the money I was hoping you  give me some direction tips from in the  right direction hope to hear from you  soon Norman Norman raising capital sucks  ok it takes up a lot of your time it  doesn't let you focus on your operations  and you get killed on the valuation now  first of all if you're only raising  $5,000 really the people who should be  talking to our friends and family it's  called love money you're not going to go  out and get an investor to put 5k into  your business you may be able to  crowdsource fund it on sites like  Kickstarter but really at that low  amount you're looking at friends and  family people who are in your network  you know even distant friends who you  haven't connected with in a while can  often be great sources but I don't think  you need the money you got to just start  up start with a service start talking to  customers get them to see the value that  you can provide and help you build a  business around their needs if you've  been wanting to start a business for  three years you got to just start it I  don't want you to wait another three  years another three years and you end up  in some job you know stuck in corporate  life and you're not you're never able to  break free of it get started start small  start a service go talk to your  potential customers find out what they  need help with and build a product or  service around them you don't need  software you don't need coaching just  start talking to your customers here's a  flip side okay if you say I really need  this money what's going to happen you  need to spend a lot of time to go out  and talk to these potential investors  right if it's your friends or family or  even if you try to get in  so is interested which is going to be  really hard for 5k you're going to take  so much of your time doing this when  instead of pitching investors you could  be pitching customers next you don't  even know if this ideas going to work or  not okay going to pitch investors with  just an idea rarely works they could put  money in and you could lose your shirt  and you're going to lose their money and  imagine you borrowed money from your  uncle or your sister or whoever it is  some distant friend of yours it doesn't  work out you're going to feel pretty  guilty I don't want that for you it's  better to invest the time into  understanding your customers and seeing  what they want so that when you actually  go and raise money it's to build it  around something that there's a need for  people have said hey I really want this  help me and the third thing is you're  going to get killed in your valuation if  you're giving up equity in your business  they're going to take a huge chunk  because it's risky what are they buying  nothing I promise a dream when you go  out and raise money you want to do it on  the best terms possible and that's going  to come after you have some momentum the  easiest type of money to raise and the  cheapest is expansion capital you've  shown that you can you can build  something up on your own you may not be  making huge money it's not glamorous but  you've shown that people will pay you  for what you do once you've proven that  you've separated yourself from  ninety-nine point nine percent of all  the other businesses that investors will  see I used to be in the venture capital  game and most of the people who gave us  their business plan had nothing had an  idea and those guys are not the ones who  got funded the guys who got funded were  the ones who already had some momentum  they already had their product or  service bill they already had people  using it some people paying them they  had proof of concept they had momentum  and they needed money to expand that's  where you want to get to it's entirely  possible to bootstrap this up spend your  time talking to customers not even  selling them just getting to know them  getting to know their pain points  understanding how you can help them and  have your customers help finance the  start of your business if it's around a  service it's just your time you don't  need anything you don't need software  you don't need consulting just get out  there and start talking to customers and  they'll guide you along your path  good luck for those of you watching you  like this video please give it a thumbs  up below makes me want to do more for  you and hey do you have a comment about  this video I'd love to hear from you  leave it in the comment section below or  if you have a question about your  business I always read those I really  loved seeing the questions and comments  come in every morning so thank you guys  and I'll see you on the next episode
 

